{
  "id": "quiz",
  "title": "Array Literals Indexing and length Check",
  "description": "Predict indexes, missing slots, and how .length changes.",
  "lessonId": "01.9.1-array-literals-indexing-and-length",
  "graphIndex": "01.9.1",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "prompt": "Given `const fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"];` what is `fruits[0]`?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "`\"banana\"`" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "`\"apple\"`" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "`\"cherry\"`" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "`undefined`" }
      ],
      "correctOptionId": "b",
      "explanation": "Array indexes start at `0`. The first element is `fruits[0]` → `\"apple\"`."
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "prompt": "Given `const fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"];` what is `fruits[3]`?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "`\"cherry\"`" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "`null`" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "`undefined`" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "Throws a RangeError" }
      ],
      "correctOptionId": "c",
      "explanation": "A missing index returns `undefined` — it does not throw."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "prompt": "Given `const fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"];` what is `fruits.length`?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "`2`" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "`3`" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "`4`" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "`\"3\"`" }
      ],
      "correctOptionId": "b",
      "explanation": "`.length` is the number of elements the array reports. Three items → `3`."
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "prompt": "How do you read the **last** element of a non-empty array `arr`?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "`arr[arr.length]`" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "`arr[arr.length - 1]`" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "`arr[-1]`" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "`arr[length]`" }
      ],
      "correctOptionId": "b",
      "explanation": "Valid indexes run `0` … `length - 1`. `arr[arr.length]` is out of range and yields `undefined`."
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "prompt": "After `const xs = [1, 2, 3]; xs[3] = 4;` what is `xs.length`?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "`3`" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "`4`" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "`5`" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "`undefined`" }
      ],
      "correctOptionId": "b",
      "explanation": "Writing past the end extends the array. `xs[3] = 4` appends one item and grows `.length` to `4`."
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "prompt": "After `const letters = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"]; letters.length = 2;` what is `letters[2]`?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "`\"c\"`" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "`\"d\"`" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "`undefined`" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "`null`" }
      ],
      "correctOptionId": "c",
      "explanation": "Shortening `.length` truncates the array. Indexes `2` and beyond are gone → `undefined`."
    }
  ]
}
